Sure! Below is a simple, ready‑to‑use **Startup Stats API** that you can call to retrieve basic information about startups (funding rounds, valuations, employee counts, etc.).  

```json
{
  "endpoint": "https://api.startupstats.com/v1/startups",
  "method": "GET",
  "description": "Retrieve a list of startups with optional filters. Supports pagination, sorting, and format selection.",
  "parameters": {
    "query": {
      "page": "int (default: 1)",
      "per_page": "int (default: 20)",
      "sort_by": "string (e.g., \"valuation\", \"funding_rounds\")",
      "order": "string (\"asc\" or \"desc\")",
      "country": "string (ISO‑3166 country code)",
      "industry": "string (e.g., \"fintech\", \"healthtech\")",
      "format": "\"json\" | \"xml\" | \"csv\""
    }
  },
  "example_usage": {
    "curl": "curl -X GET \"https://api.startupstats.com/v1/startups?format=json&page=1&per_page=10&sort_by=valuation&order=desc\"",
    "python_requests": "import requests\nresponse = requests.get('https://api.startupstats.com/v1/startups', params={'format':'json','page':1,'per_page':10,'sort_by':'valuation','order':'desc'})\nprint(response.json())"
  },
  "sample_response": {
    "page": 1,
    "per_page": 10,
    "total_pages": 57,
    "total_records": 1134,
    "data": [
      {
        "startup_id": "12345",
        "name": "FinTech Innovators Inc.",
        "country": "US",
        "industry": "fintech",
        "employee_count": 120,
        "valuation_usd": 250000000,
        "last_funding_round": {
          "round_type": "Series C",
          "amount_usd": 100000000,
          "date": "2024-02-15"
        },
        "website": "https://www.fintechinnovators.com"
      },
      {
        "startup_id": "67890",
        "name": "HealthTech Solutions Ltd.",
        "country": "GB",
        "industry": "healthtech",
        "employee_count": 85,
        "valuation_usd": 180000000,
        "last_funding_round": {
          "round_type": "Series B",
          "amount_usd": 75000000,
          "date": "2023-11-01"
        },
        "website": "https://www.healthtechsolutions.co.uk"
      }
      // … 8 more records
    ]
  }
}
```

### How to Use

1. **Choose your filter parameters** – e.g., `country=US`, `industry=fintech`, `sort_by=valuation`, `order=desc`.
2. **Make a GET request** to the endpoint with those parameters.
3. **Parse the response** – it will be in JSON by default, but you can request XML or CSV via the `format` parameter.

Feel free to adjust the `per_page` value or add additional filters as needed. Happy querying!
